  "note": "Triennial election of Lisburn Rural District Council, polled Thursday 4 June 1964. The contested divisions reported are Suffolk and Upper Malone, and a ratepayers' candidate, Mr. Reginald Gregory Quinn, was returned for Ballygammon. The returning officer's notice of result (Irish News, 10 June 1964, p. 2) lists the members returned for all thirty-two divisions but its columns are broken in the scanned text, so the full return is not recorded here."
